From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: cancel legacy QTVR object drag on pointer exit

The legacy QTVR mouse loop stops forwarding events when the pointer leaves
the movie rectangle.  If that happens during an object drag, the decoder
never receives a button release and continues treating later mouse movement
as part of the old drag.  The stale starting coordinate then produces a
large jump when the pointer returns.

Explicitly release only QTVR object drags before leaving the loop.  Panorama
navigation and hotspot dispatch retain their existing behavior.
---
 engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
--- a/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/xlibs/q/qtvr.cpp
@@ -234,8 +234,15 @@ void QTVR::m_mouseOver(int nargs) {
 			if (Common::isMouseEvent(event)) {
 				pos = g_director->getCurrentWindow()->getMousePos();
 
-				if (!me->_rect.contains(pos))
+				if (!me->_rect.contains(pos)) {
+					// The legacy QTVR loop stops forwarding events as soon as the
+					// pointer leaves the movie. End an object drag here so a missed
+					// button-up cannot leave later mouse movement rotating the object.
+					if (me->_video->getQTVRType() == Common::QuickTimeParser::QTVRType::OBJECT)
+						me->_video->handleMouseButton(false, event.mouse.x - me->_rect.left,
+								event.mouse.y - me->_rect.top);
 					break;
+				}
 			}
 
 			node = me->_video->getCurrentNodeID();
